# graphify — the knowledge-graph output (graphify update .) is COMMITTED as of
# v0.37.2, so agents and CI can read the graph without regenerating it (CLAUDE.md
# tells agents to read GRAPH_REPORT.md before answering architecture questions).
# Only the regenerable cache and the local interpreter marker stay ignored.
# Trade-off, accepted deliberately: graph.json is multi-MB, so `graphify update .`
# produces large diffs and the blobs are permanent in history.
**/graphify-out/cache/
.graphify_python

# Claude Code — personal/machine-local settings only. `.claude/settings.json` is the
# committable, team-shared wiring file (deliberately NOT ignored) — it stays untracked
# for now because it still carries the token-capture hooks that Phase 2 removes.
.claude/settings.local.json

